# fixedbugs, defect 2372, lane b26-cli, 2026-11-09.
#
# The header defines `top2372` `static inline`, its body calling
# `base2372_helper`, which the header declares and nothing on the link line
# defines. The reference stands in this program's own object, compiled from
# the header's text, so until 2026-11-09 every linker's refusal was told
# *internal error: linking failed* at exit 2. The header is now asked
# whether its text names the name, and the binding that brings the body in
# is told, with the `link` the program needs, this group's own first.

extern "fixedbugs-2372-fast.h"
    function top2372() -> i32  #~ ffi_missing_link

function main()
    print(top2372())
